messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nSymphony No. 9 is a music piece. Composers write music pieces. Beethoven wrote Symphony No. 9. Vienna Music Society premiered Symphony No. 9. Vienna Music Society is an orchestra. Beethoven leads the Vienna Music Society. Orchestras are led by conductors.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Beethoven is a composer.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Beethoven is a composer" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me start by reading through the context carefully.\n\nThe context says that symphonies are written by composers, and specifically, Beethoven wrote Symphony No. 9. It also mentions that the Vienna Music Society is an orchestra and that Beethoven leads it, with orchestras led by conductors. \n\nSo, from this, I can gather that Beethoven composed the symphony, which is a type of music piece. Since composers create music pieces, and Beethoven wrote Symphony No. 9, that makes him a composer. \n\nI don\'t see any information that contradicts this. The context doesn\'t say anything about Beethoven not being a composer or that he did something else instead. It only talks about him writing a symphony and leading an orchestra. \n\nTherefore, the statement should be true because the context directly supports it by stating that Beethoven wrote a symphony, which implies he was a composer.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because Beethoven wrote a symphony, which means he is a composer. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
