messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, let\'s list out all the given statements:.\n\n1. No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.\n2. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.\n3. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.\n4. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.\n5. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.\n6. James is a student working in the lab.\n7. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\nThe question is about James. We need to determine if it\'s true, false, or uncertain whether James does not have a part-time job.\n\nLet me start by analyzing each statement and seeing how they connect.\n\nFrom statement 5: All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab (statement 6), so James must be instructed by professor David.\n\nFrom statement 4: All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. Since James is instructed by David, he is taking the database course.\n\nFrom statement 3: All students taking the database course are from the computer science department. Therefore, James is from the computer science department.\n\nNow, statement 1: No students who work in the library are from the computer science department. Since James is from computer science, he cannot be working in the library. So, James is not in the library.\n\nStatement 2: All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. This means if a student has such a job, they must be in the library. But we know James is not in the library, so he cannot have a part-time job offered by the university. Therefore, James does not have such a job.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The statements don\'t mention anything about part-time jobs outside the library. So, the only way a student can have a part-time job is by working in the library. Since James isn\'t in the library, he can\'t have that job. So, the statement is definitely true.\n\nI think that\'s solid</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because James works in the lab, which means he\'s instructed by Professor David and thus taking the database course. Being in the computer science department, he can\'t work in the library. Since part-time jobs are only in the library, James doesn\'t have one. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
