messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the given statements to make it clearer:\n\n1. No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.\n2. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.\n3. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.\n4. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.\n5. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.\n6. James is a student working in the lab.\n7. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\nNow, the question is about James. Let\'s focus on what we know about James.\n\nFrom statement 5, James is working in the lab. Statement 4 says all students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. So, James is instructed by David.\n\nStatement 3 says all students taking the database course are from the computer science department. Since James is taking the database course (because he\'s working in the lab, and from statement 4, he\'s instructed by David, and statement 4 implies he\'s taking the database course), he must be from the computer science department.\n\nNow, statement 2 says all students with part-time jobs offered by the university work in the library. So, if James had a part-time job, he would be working in the library. But from statement 1, no students from the computer science department work in the library. Since James is from the computer science department, he cannot be working in the library. Therefore, he cannot have a part-time job offered by the university because that would require him to work in the library, which he\'s not doing.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. Let\'s see:\n\n- James works in the lab (statement 5).\n- Working in the lab means he\'s instructed by David (statement 4).\n- Being instructed by David means he\'s taking the database course (statement 4 again, but more importantly, statement 3 says database students are CS).\n- So James is a CS student taking the database course.\n- If he had a part-time job, he\'d have to work in the library (statement 2).\n- But CS students don\'t work in the library (statement 1).\n- Therefore, James cannot have a part-time job because that would put him in the library, which is impossible.\n\nSo, the conclusion is that James does not have a part-time job offered by the university. Therefore, the statement is false.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is false because James, being a computer science student, cannot work in the library, so he doesn\'t have a part-time job. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
