messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAll squares have four sides. All four-sided things are shapes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? All squares are shapes.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "All squares are shapes" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context provided says two things: "All squares have four sides" and "All four-sided things are shapes." So, I need to see how these two statements relate to each other and how they apply to the question.\n\nLet me start by understanding each part. The first statement is about squares—they have four sides. That makes sense because, by definition, a square is a quadrilateral, which means it has four sides. So, every square fits this description.\n\nThe second statement says that all four-sided things are shapes. Hmm, so if something has four sides, it\'s considered a shape. That seems a bit broad, but I guess in this context, they\'re defining shapes as any four-sided figure. So, a square, which is four-sided, would fall under this category.\n\nNow, the question is asking if all squares are shapes. From the context, since all four-sided things are shapes, and squares are four-sided, it follows that squares must be shapes. So, if every four-sided thing is a shape, and squares are four-sided, then squares are definitely shapes.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The context doesn\'t mention anything about shapes beyond four sides. So, are there other criteria for being a shape? Well, in the given context, the only definition provided is that four-sided things are shapes. So, based solely on that, squares being four-sided would make them shapes.\n\nI don\'t think there\'s any uncertainty here because the context gives clear premises. Therefore, the statement "All squares are shapes" must be true based on the given information.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement "All squares are shapes" is true because squares, having four sides, are categorized as shapes according to the provided context. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
