messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Tom can apply for financial aid from ETS to take the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Tom can apply for financial aid from ETS to take the GRE test" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that it costs $205 to take the GRE test, and ETS offers financial aid to applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship is defined as difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom is a single-parent living with his dad, who has been out of work for more than a year. \n\nSo, the key points here are Tom\'s economic situation and whether ETS\'s criteria for financial aid are met. Since Tom\'s dad has been out of work for over a year, Tom is likely experiencing financial hardship because he doesn\'t have an income. He\'s a single parent, so he\'s probably managing with whatever little money he has, which might not be enough to pay the $205 fee. \n\nNow, the question is whether Tom can apply for this financial aid. The context doesn\'t specify any additional requirements beyond proving economic hardship. It just mentions that ETS provides aid to those who can demonstrate such hardship. Therefore, as long as Tom can show that he\'s experiencing economic hardship, he should be eligible.\n\nHowever, I should consider if there are any implicit factors. For example, does Tom have any means test or other documentation requirements? The context doesn\'t mention anything like that, so it\'s safe to assume that the only requirement is proving economic hardship, which Tom seems to have.\n\nTherefore, the statement should be true because Tom meets the criteria for financial aid based on his economic situation.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because Tom, being a single-parent with an unemployed father, likely faces economic hardship, making him eligible for ETS\'s financial aid. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
