messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nSome basketball players are not American. All basketball players are tall. If someone is tall, they wear large shoes. If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes. Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If Yuri does not wear large shoes, then Yuri is an American basketball player.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out this logic problem. Let me read through the context and the question again to make sure I understand everything.\n\nThe context says:.\n1. Some basketball players are not American.\n2. All basketball players are tall.\n3. If someone is tall, they wear large shoes.\n4. If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes.\n5. Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.\n\nThe question is: Based on this information, is the statement "If Yuri does not wear large shoes, then Yuri is an American basketball player." True, false, or uncertain?.\n\nAlright, let\'s break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, let\'s outline the given information:.\n\n- Some basketball players are not American. So, there\'s a subset of basketball players who are American, and another subset who are not. But we don\'t know how big these subsets are.\n\n- All basketball players are tall. So, every basketball player, regardless of being American or not, is tall.\n\n- If someone is tall, they wear large shoes. So, being tall is a necessary condition for wearing large shoes. In logical terms, tall → large shoes.\n\n- If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes. So, large shoes → large clothes.\n\n- Yuri does not wear large-size clothes. So, ¬large clothes.\n\nNow, the statement we need to evaluate is: If Yuri does not wear large shoes (¬large shoes), t