apply for CPT or OPT.\n\nTherefore, while it\'s possible that Mike has an F1 visa because he needs CPT, we can\'t be certain because the context doesn\'t exclude the possibility that he might have a J1 visa and still needs CPT for some reason. So, the statement "Mike has an F1 visa" is uncertain because the given information doesn\'t definitively confirm his visa type.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is uncertain because the context doesn\'t confirm Mike\'s visa type beyond knowing he has either F1 or J1, and while F1 requires CPT, J1\'s requirements aren\'t specified. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
