messages:   49%|####9     | 100/204 [00:27<00:41,  2.48it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nNo digital media are analog. Every printed text is analog. All streaming services are digital. If an object is a hardcover book then it is printed text. If 1984 is a streaming service, then 1984 is a hardcover book.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? 1984 is not a streaming service.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "1984 is not a streaming service" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that no digital media are analog. That means if something is digital, it\'s not analog, and vice versa. Then it mentions that every printed text is analog. So printed books, for example, are analog media.\n\nNext, it states that all streaming services are digital. So if something is a streaming service, it must be digital. That makes sense because streaming services like Netflix or Spotify are digital platforms.\n\nThen there\'s a conditional statement: If an object is a hardcover book, then it is printed text. So hardcover books are a subset of printed texts. Since printed texts are analog, hardcover books are also analog.\n\nNow, the last statement is a bit more complex: If 1984 is a streaming service, then 1984 is a hardcover book. Let me parse this. This is an "if-then" statement, so it\'s saying that if 1984 is a streaming service, then it must be a hardcover book. But wait, we know that streaming services are digital, and hardcover books are analog. So if 1984 were a streaming service, it would have to be digital, but hardcover books are analog. That creates a contradiction because a streaming service can\'t be a hardcover book.\n\nSo, putting it all together: If 1984 is a streaming service, then it\'s a hardcover book (which is analog). But since streaming services are digital, 1984 can\'t be both digital and analog at the same time. Therefore, the only way to avoid this contradiction is if 1984 is not a streaming service. Because if it were, it would have to be a hardcover book, which is impossible given the nature of streaming services being digital.\n\nSo, the statement "1984 is not a streaming service" must be true because assuming it is a streaming service leads to a logical contradiction</think>.\n\nThe statement "1984 is not a streaming service" is true because if it were a streaming service, it would have to be a hardcover book, which is impossible since streaming services are digital and hardcover books are analog. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
