s things a bit. However, the key here is that Platypus are mammals, even though they don\'t have teeth. So, the fact that some mammals have teeth doesn\'t exclude the possibility that others, like Humans, also have teeth. \n\nTherefore, based on the information given, Humans are indeed mammals because they fall under the category of mammals that have teeth. The presence of teeth is a characteristic of mammals, and since Humans have teeth, they must be mammals. \n\nI don\'t see any information in the context that would suggest otherwise. Platypus being mammals without teeth doesn\'t affect the classification of Humans. So, the statement should be true.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement "Humans are mammals" is supported by the context, as Humans have teeth, which is a characteristic of mammals. Therefore, the statement is true. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
