messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Stranger Things" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Karen will share \'Stranger Things\' to Lisa" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context tells me that "Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. Then, it says that if a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. So, since "Stranger Things" is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. Got that.\n\nNext, the context mentions that Karen will download a Netflix show only if and only if she binge-watches it. So, the act of downloading is directly tied to her binge-watching. Since she\'s going to binge-watch "Stranger Things," she will download it. That makes sense.\n\nNow, the context also states that Karen does not download "Black Mirror," and it\'s mentioned that "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. But since "Stranger Things" is a different show, and we know she will download it, this fact about "Black Mirror" doesn\'t affect her downloading of "Stranger Things." So, that\'s probably just additional info to set up the scenario.\n\nThen, there\'s another part that says if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa. So, since she\'s going to binge-watch "Stranger Things," she will share it with Lisa.\n\nPutting it all together: "Stranger Things" is popular → Karen bingewatches it → Karen downloads it → Karen shares it with Lisa. Therefore, the statement should be true.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because Karen will share "Stranger Things" with Lisa based on the given conditions. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
