it was translated from Italian by New Vessel Press, which only publishes English books, the final version of Neapolitan Chronicles is in English. Therefore, the statement that Neapolitan Chronicles is an English book should be true.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The context says all of New Vessel Press\'s books are in English, so regardless of the original language, they are translated into English. So, even though it was originally in Italian, after translation, it\'s English. Therefore, the statement is definitely true.\n\nI don\'t think there\'s any uncertainty here because the context provides clear information about New Vessel Press\'s publishing activity</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because Neapolitan Chronicles was published by New Vessel Press, which translates foreign literature into English. Therefore, it is an English book. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
