messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nA podcast is not a novel. [BG] If a person is born in American City, the person is American. [BG] If a book is novel and it is written by a person, then the person is a novel writer. Dani Shapiro is an American writer. Family History is written by Dani Shapiro. Family History is a novel written in 2003. Dani Shapiro created a podcast called Family Secrets. [BG] Boston is an American city.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Dani Shapiro is a novel writer.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Dani Shapiro is a novel writer" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because Dani Shapiro wrote a novel, Family History, which makes her a novel writer. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
