messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that on some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. So, that means there are Mondays at 8 pm where roses are on TV. But roses are given out on TV, and every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. So, if roses are on TV on those Mondays, they\'re part of the Bachelor.\n\nNext, it says that every show on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. So, the Bachelor is a show that depicts real people\'s lives. Then, it mentions that all shows that portray real people are reality TV shows. So, the Bachelor is a reality TV show because it shows real lives.\n\nNow, the context goes on to say that Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show. So, Breaking Bad doesn\'t fall into the category of reality TV shows. \n\nThe question is asking if Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm. Let\'s see. The context tells us that roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm, and those are on the Bachelor. Since the Bachelor is a reality TV show, and Breaking Bad isn\'t a reality TV show, it can\'t be on the Bachelor. Therefore, Breaking Bad can\'t be on those Mondays at 8 pm because those are reserved for the Bachelor.\n\nWait, but the context doesn\'t say that all Mondays at 8 pm are only for the Bachelor. It just says that on some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV, which are on the Bachelor. So, it\'s possible that other shows air on TV on Mondays at 8 pm, but the ones that are on the Bachelor are the ones with roses. Breaking Bad isn\'t on the Bachelor, so it\'s not on those specific Mondays at 8 pm.\n\nTherefore, the statement that Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm is false because it\'s not a reality TV show and thus not on the Bachelor, which is the only place those Mondays at 8 pm are used for.\n</think>.\n\nBreaking Bad is not a reality TV show, so it cannot be on the Bachelor, which is the only show on Mondays at 8 pm. Therefore, the statement is false. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
