messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nInternational students in US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa. An international student in US with an F1 visa needs to apply for CPT or OPT if the student wants to work in the US. Mike is an international student. Mike needs to apply for CPT if he wants to work in the US.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mike has a J1 visa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Mike has a J1 visa" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that international students in the US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa. So, Mike, being an international student, must have one of these two visas. That means Mike\'s visa is either F1 or J1.\n\nNext, the context mentions that an international student with an F1 visa needs to apply for either CPT or OPT if they want to work in the US. So, if Mike wants to work in the US, he must have an F1 visa and thus needs to apply for CPT or OPT.\n\nThe question is asking about Mike\'s visa type. The statement claims he has a J1 visa. But from the context, we only know that he has either F1 or J1. The fact that he needs to apply for CPT or OPT indicates he has an F1 visa. Therefore, he can\'t have a J1 visa because J1 doesn\'t require applying for CPT or OPT for work.\n\nSo, based on this reasoning, the statement that Mike has a J1 visa must be false because he must have an F1 visa to be able to work in the US.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is false because Mike has an F1 visa, as indicated by his need to apply for CPT or OPT to work in the US. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
