messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test." is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me start by reading the context carefully.\n\nThe context says that it costs US $205 to take the GRE test. Then it mentions that ETS provides financial aid to those applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship is defined as difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom is an example given; he lives in a single-parent family, and his dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\nThe question is asking about the cost of taking the GRE test. The statement in question is whether the cost is below $300. The context directly states that the cost is $205. So, $205 is definitely below $300. Therefore, the statement should be true.\n\nI don\'t think there\'s any uncertainty here because the context provides a clear and specific number. Even though the context also talks about financial aid for those in economic hardship, that doesn\'t affect the cost of the test itself. The financial aid is a separate benefit provided by ETS, but the cost remains at $205 regardless of whether someone qualifies for aid or not.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the cost is $205, which is below $300, making the statement true. There\'s no ambiguity or missing information that would make this uncertain</think>.\n\nThe cost of taking the GRE test is explicitly stated as $205, which is below $300. Therefore, the statement is true. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
