messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Breaking Bad is a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm." is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context tells me a few things:\n\n1. On some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV.\n2. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor.\n3. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n4. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n5. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\nNow, the question is about whether Breaking Bad is a TV show where roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm. Let\'s see how these pieces connect.\n\nStarting with point 1: Roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm. So, if a show has roses given out on TV on those specific times, it\'s part of this category.\n\nPoint 2 says every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. So, any show that gives out roses on TV must be on the Bachelor.\n\nPoint 3: Everything on the Bachelor portrays real people. So, the Bachelor is a show that portrays real people.\n\nPoint 4: All shows that portray real people are reality TV shows. Therefore, the Bachelor is a reality TV show because it portrays real people.\n\nPoint 5: Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show. So, Breaking Bad doesn\'t fall into the category of reality TV shows.\n\nNow, putting this together: Since the Bachelor is a reality TV show (from points 3 and 4), and Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show (point 5), Breaking Bad cannot be on the Bachelor. Therefore, Breaking Bad doesn\'t have roses given out on TV because if it did, it would have to be on the Bachelor, which it\'s not.\n\nSo, the statement that Breaking Bad is a TV show where roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm is false because it\'s not on the Bachelor, and thus doesn\'t have those roses.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is false because Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show, so it can\'t be on the Bachelor, which is where roses are given out. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
