messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nRobert Lewandowski is a striker. [BG] Strikers are soccer players. Robert Lewandowski left Bayern Munchen. [BG] If a player left a team they no longer play for that team.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Robert Lewandowski is a soccer player.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Robert Lewandowski is a soccer player" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, looking at the context provided:\n\n1. Robert Lewandowski is a striker. \n2. Strikers are soccer players.\n3. Robert Lewandowski left Bayern Munchen.\n4. If a player leaves a team, they no longer play for that team.\n\nNow, the question is about whether Robert Lewandowski is a soccer player. Let\'s see how the context connects.\n\nFrom point 1, he\'s a striker. From point 2, strikers are soccer players. So that directly connects him to being a soccer player. The fact that he left his team in point 3 doesn\'t change his status as a soccer player; it just means he\'s no longer associated with that particular team. So, his status as a soccer player remains intact.\n\nI don\'t see any information that would suggest he\'s not a soccer player. The only change is that he\'s no longer at Bayern Munchen, but that doesn\'t affect his profession. Therefore, the statement should be true.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because Robert Lewandowski is a striker, and strikers are soccer players. His departure from a team doesn\'t change his status. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
