 in Montana. So, Pierre must be in a different state. Therefore, Butte and Pierre cannot be in the same state.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The context doesn\'t mention any other states besides Montana, except for Pierre being in a different place. So, Pierre is definitely not in Montana, and since Butte is in Montana, they can\'t be in the same state.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the statement "Butte and Pierre are in the same state" must be false because Butte is in Montana, and Pierre is not in Montana.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is false because Butte is in Montana, while Pierre is not in Montana, so they cannot be in the same state. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
