on\'t provide any information about whether all gentlemen are CEOs or not. So, Harry being a gentleman doesn\'t automatically make him a CEO. There could be other gentlemen who are not CEOs, and Harry could be one of them. Therefore, we can\'t definitively say he\'s a CEO; it\'s uncertain.\n\nI think that\'s the right approach. The key point is that the premises don\'t establish a bi-conditional relationship between being a gentleman and being a CEO. So, Harry could be a CEO, but he might not be. We don\'t have enough information to confirm either way.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement "Harry is a CEO" is uncertain because the premises only establish that all CEOs are gentlemen, but they don\'t confirm that all gentlemen are CEOs. Harry being a gentleman doesn\'t necessarily make him a CEO. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
