in humans or whether anyone gets it. It only talks about Monkeypox, its causes, and symptoms.\n\nSo, the statement "No one gets flu." is making a general claim about flu, but the context doesn\'t provide any information to support or refute that claim. There\'s no data on flu rates, whether it\'s common, rare, or nonexistent. The context is entirely about Monkeypox, not about flu.\n\nTherefore, since the context doesn\'t provide any information about flu, the statement\'s truthfulness can\'t be determined. It\'s uncertain because we don\'t have enough data to confirm or deny it.\n</think>.\n\nThe statement "No one gets flu." is uncertain because the context provided does not offer any information about flu, making it impossible to confirm or deny the statement. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
