messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock has wings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Rock has wings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context tells me that all mammals are animals. Then, all monkeys are mammals, so monkeys are also animals. It also says that an animal is either a monkey or a bird. Wait, so every animal is either a monkey or a bird? That means there are no other animals outside of these two categories. So, if something is an animal, it must be a monkey or a bird.\n\nNext, all birds fly. So, every bird has wings because they can fly. Then, all animals breathe, which is a general fact. .\n\nNow, there\'s a conditional statement: If something can fly, then it has wings. That makes sense because flying usually requires wings. So, flying implies wings.\n\nThen, the last part says, "If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes." Hmm, that\'s a bit tricky. Let me parse that. So, Rock is not a fly, and Rock is not a bird. From the previous statements, since all animals are either monkeys or birds, and all birds fly, if Rock is an animal, it would have to be a monkey or a bird, which would mean it flies. But Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, so Rock isn\'t an animal. Therefore, Rock isn\'t an animal, so it can\'t be a monkey or a bird.\n\nBut wait, the statement says if Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock isn\'t a fly, and Rock isn\'t a bird. From the previous information, since all animals are either monkeys or birds, if Rock were an animal, it would have to be a monkey or a bird, which would mean it flies. But Rock isn\'t a fly or a bird, so Rock isn\'t an animal. Therefore, Rock isn\'t an animal, so it can\'t be a monkey or a bird. .\n\nBut the conclusion is that Rock neither flies nor breathes. Wait, but all animals breathe, so if Rock isn\'t an animal, does that mean it doesn\'t breathe? Or is there another possibility? Let me think.\n\nThe statement says, "If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes." So, Rock isn\'t a fly, and Rock isn\'t a bird. From the context, since all animals are either monkeys or birds, Rock isn\'t an animal. So, Rock isn\'t a monkey or a bird, which are animals. Therefore, Rock isn\'t an animal, so it doesn\'t breathe because all animals breathe. Wait, but the statement says that if Rock isn\'t a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn\'t fly (given) and doesn\'t breathe (because it\'s not an animal). .\n\nBut the question is about whether Rock has wings. From the context, all birds fly and have wings. Since Rock isn\'t a bird, it doesn\'t have wings. So, Rock doesn\'t fly, and since it\'s not a bird, it doesn\'t have wings either. .\n\nWait, but the statement says that if Rock isn\'t a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn\'t fly, and it doesn\'t breathe. But the question is about wings. Since Rock isn\'t a bird, it doesn\'t have wings. So, Rock doesn\'t have wings. .\n\nBut let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The context says all animals are either monkeys or birds, so Rock isn\'t an animal. Therefore, Rock isn\'t a monkey or a bird. Since all birds fly, Rock isn\'t a bird, so it doesn\'t fly. The statement also says that if Rock isn\'t a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn\'t fly, and it doesn\'t breathe. .\n\nBut the question is about wings. Since Rock isn\'t a bird, it doesn\'t have wings. So, Rock doesn\'t have wings. Therefore, the statement "Rock has wings" would be false. .\n\nWait, but the last part says that if Rock isn\'t a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn\'t fly, and it doesn\'t breathe. But the question is about wings, which are related to flying. Since Rock isn\'t a bird, it doesn\'t have wings. So, Rock doesn\'t have wings. .\n\nSo, the answer should be that Rock does not have wings, making the statement "Rock has wings" false</think>.\n\nThe statement "Rock has wings" is false because Rock is neither a bird nor a fly, and since all birds have wings, Rock cannot have wings. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 97%|#########7| 198/204 [01:12<00:01,  5.60it/s]
